{
 "id": "threads/model-switch-unreported/main-joins-subagent-model",
 "description": "Main runs on the large model and a subagent on the small one, each with its own cache entry. Main moves to the small model and nothing reports it: the request names a different model from main's previous one, and the provider keeps a cache for each model, so main reads nothing and writes all 31,000 tokens. The library sees the loss from the usage and records a break nobody caused, 30,000 tokens from read to write, labelled model_changed. It is in the client body's bill too, so the baseline equals the bill and the break nets out. The cmdfilter saving after B* is a write, 7,000 x $1.00. The subagent's own thread is untouched. cg's seenModel is keyed by model alone, so main's first request on the small model is not a cold start: the subagent used it first.",
 "source": "issue_cases.md#423",
